  "usage": {
    "summary": "`good-pdf-preview` displays one PDF page at a time inside a responsive GoodUI frame. Its toolbar owns page navigation, zoom (50–300% of fitted width), clockwise rotation, and an optional download action. The document viewport scrolls when a zoomed page exceeds its width. PDF.js renders the page and a selectable text layer; page count updates are announced to assistive technology. `PageUp` and `PageDown` work while the viewport has focus.",
